On Fri, Mar 5, 2010 at 11:44 AM, Michael Turniansky
<mturniansky@gmail.com> wrote:
> On Fri, Mar 5, 2010 at 9:37 AM, Jonathan Jones <eyeonus@gmail.com> wrote:
>> I would guess that the reason for the {se ... fa} bit was partly to
>> emphasize the experience and partly to keep from having to figure out how to
>> terminate {lonu zutse ne'i le ricyzda gi'enai tavla}
>
> ??  It just terminates with a single kei (which, if it was moved to
> the front, wouldn't even be needed if cu was there.)

"kei" by itself wouldn't work in this case. "kei" terminates "nu", but
not "lo", so "lo nu zutse ne'i le ricyzda gi'enai tavla kei zifre" is
just a sumti. "ku" would be the needed terminator in this case, but of
course "cu" is better. "cu" is always better than terminators.

It still makes sense to move a heavy x1 sumti after the selbri just
for clarity, so that you don't keep the listener wondering what the
selbri will be until the last minute.

